29:["$","article",null,{"className":"bg-card border border-border rounded-3xl p-6 sm:p-12 shadow-xs prose dark:prose-invert max-w-none","children":[["$","h1","1",{"className":"text-2xl sm:text-3xl font-black text-foreground mt-8 mb-4 tracking-tight","children":"The Speed Dynasty: Redefining the Sevens Wing"}],["$","p","3",{"className":"text-base sm:text-lg text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed my-4","children":"For nearly a decade, opposing teams on the World Rugby Sevens Series shared a single, terrifying tactical concern: do not give Perry Baker or Carlin Isles an inch of open prairie."}],["$","h2","5",{"className":"text-xl sm:text-2xl font-bold text-foreground mt-8 mb-3 tracking-tight border-b border-border/50 pb-2","children":"Perry Baker: The Magician from Daytona Beach"}],["$","p","7",{"className":"text-base sm:text-lg text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed my-4","children":"Perry Baker wasn't merely fast; he possessed arguably the most deceptive acceleration and balanced swerve in rugby history. Twice awarded World Rugby Men's Sevens Player of the Year (2017 and 2018), Baker accumulated more than 290 career series tries, breaking ankles and game plans alike."}],["$","p","9",{"className":"text-base sm:text-lg text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed my-4","children":"His ability to read defensive spacing, chip and chase, and recover his own kicks made him a complete three-dimensional threat on both sides of the ball."}],["$","h2","11",{"className":"text-xl sm:text-2xl font-bold text-foreground mt-8 mb-3 tracking-tight border-b border-border/50 pb-2","children":"Carlin Isles: The Fastest Man in Rugby"}],["$","p","13",{"className":"text-base sm:text-lg text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed my-4","children":"Hailing from Massillon, Ohio, Carlin Isles arrived in rugby with a 10.13-second 100-meter track pedigree. What initially looked like an intriguing athletic crossover rapidly turned into a clinical finishing showcase. Opposing sweepers had to adjust their defensive lines by 15 meters simply to account for his straight-line velocity."}],["$","h2","15",{"className":"text-xl sm:text-2xl font-bold text-foreground mt-8 mb-3 tracking-tight border-b border-border/50 pb-2","children":"Tactical Impact on Modern Sevens"}],["$","p","17",{"className":"text-base sm:text-lg text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed my-4","children":"Together with cerebral playmakers like Madison Hughes, Danny Barrett, and Folau Niua, the Baker-Isles era proved that American athletic crossover potential could dominate Tier-1 rugby nations when matched with world-class skill development."}]]}]
